From 31598561a2aad268efd67413952b6dac27d69a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke <lukeserventi2000@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Nov 2026 20:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] halium.config: enable CONFIG_PM_AUTOSLEEP for repowerd libsuspend

The GKI build lost CONFIG_PM_AUTOSLEEP (stock Android has it). Runtime
proof on husky 2026-11-20: /sys/power/autosleep is ENOENT and android
libsuspend init probe (write "on" to /sys/power/state) returns EINVAL,
so repowerd logs "Failed to initialize libsuspend" every boot and falls
back to LogindSystemPowerControl (no wakelock-gated autosuspend).

Adds CONFIG_PM_AUTOSLEEP=y to the EFFECTIVE GKI defconfig fragment
(arch/arm64/configs/halium.config, consumed per aosp/0013). CONFIG_PM_
WAKELOCKS is already effective (/sys/power/wake_lock exists), untouched.

Phase 2 change-set; validate on device before promoting (see
husky-verify/phase2-power-usability.md): /sys/power/autosleep present,
repowerd starts LibsuspendSystemPowerControl, known-good suite unchanged.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/halium.config | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config b/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
index 68818c3f3a76..81d408b1cbc6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
@@ -40,3 +40,10 @@
 
 # USB networking (RNDIS) for SSH debugging over USB
 CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_RNDIS=y
+
+# Android autosuspend (libsuspend): repowerd LibsuspendSystemPowerControl
+# probe-writes "on" to /sys/power/state and requires /sys/power/autosleep.
+# Our GKI config dropped it -> EINVAL probe -> repowerd falls back to logind
+# suspend (no wakelock-gated autosuspend). See husky-verify
+# phase2-power-usability.md (Phase 2). Tested missing on device 2026-11-20.
+CONFIG_PM_AUTOSLEEP=y
-- 
